content.text:
Confirmed: this commit introduces `failedRemoveCinderDisks` initialized to `null`, then calls `failedRemoveCinderDisks.addAll(cinderDisks)` on the exception path — a guaranteed NPE if `future.get()` throws `InterruptedException`/`ExecutionException`.

## Bug-Introducing Commits
BIC: 1bfc9d0cc2e5e3a61fe3985d74b44efc6d6366a4

## Reasoning

**(1) Investigation:** I traced the history of `RemoveVmCommand.java` around the `failedRemoveCinderDisks` variable using `git log -S"failedRemoveCinderDisks"` (pickaxe search), which finds the commit that introduced the string. This returned a single commit: `1bfc9d0cc2e5e3a61fe3985d74b44efc6d6366a4` ("core: Support remove of VM with Cinder disks"), which also appears in the recent commit log provided in the initial context — one commit prior to the fix (`ae33192d31`) in the log.

**(2) Specific bug:** In commit `1bfc9d0cc`, the new `removeCinderDisks()` method declares:
```java
Collection<CinderDisk> failedRemoveCinderDisks = null;
...
try {
    failedRemoveCinderDisks = future.get().getActionReturnValue();
} catch (InterruptedException | ExecutionException e) {
    failedRemoveCinderDisks.addAll(cinderDisks);   // NPE here
    log.error("Exception", e);
}
```
The variable starts as `null` and is only assigned inside the `try` block. If `future.get()` throws (the very case the `catch` block is meant to handle), `failedRemoveCinderDisks` is still `null` when `.addAll(...)` is invoked on it, causing a guaranteed `NullPointerException`.

**(3) Evidence:** The fix commit `ae33192d31` changes exactly this line, from `failedRemoveCinderDisks.addAll(cinderDisks);` to `failedRemoveCinderDisks = cinderDisks;`, which avoids calling a method on the null reference. `git blame`/pickaxe confirms this line, along with the variable's `null` initialization, was introduced together in `1bfc9d0cc` and untouched until the fix — no other commit modified this code path in between.

I'm confident in this attribution since the introducing and fixing commits touch the exact same line/variable with no intervening changes.

